--- a/docs/design.md
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -49,3 +49,5 @@
 Copper takes hit-test priority over component bodies in the Visual Editor. Editing trace vertices reuses drawing snap targets (same-layer traces/pads and through-vias); Shift bypasses snapping, and endpoint pad anchors update on commit.
 
 The KiCad footprint/symbol browser shows a Pins column from index metadata, counting distinct numbered electrical terminals rather than duplicate pads. Unknown legacy counts show a dash with a rescan hint.
+
+Changing an existing component footprint/symbol opens a dedicated replacement review: information fields at the top, independent side-by-side footprint/symbol search tables, paired previews, then pin assignments. It exposes Close and Apply replacement rather than create/save/place actions. Replacing one definition retains the other and preserves valid pin mappings; the content can scroll inside the fixed dialog.
